# Keep README.md current

`README.md` is the canonical project document. `docs/PROJECT.md` is only a pointer — do not put new facts there.

When a change affects any of the following, **update `README.md` in the same turn** (constants, file paths, scripts, stop count, knobs, landmines):

- Tech stack / `package.json` / Vite pages
- Camera rig, ring layout, scroll, parallax, intro drop
- Lighting, post stack (bloom / grain), neon tubes / fog bake
- Vignettes, GLB paths, screen pipelines (XP / MySpace / SMS)
- Load / boot gate, interaction lock
- npm or Python scripts, asset pipeline, Git LFS
- Dev probes (`window.__stage…`)

Rules:

- Describe **what is running**, not dead prototypes.
- Prefer numbers copied from `src/scene/stage/constants.js` and the owning module — do not invent tunables.
- If you rename a file or constant, grep README and fix every mention.
- Bump the **Last verified** date at the top of README when you edit it.
